  ],
  "description": "zk2 keys (core.md §1.1, §1.2). `expect` is the parse, or null when the key is refused. A key is parsed without a contract, so only the lexical rules apply: a resource chunk is any plain chunk. Every accepted key must build back to exactly the same string. An events key's parse adds `occurrence`: its last chunk's stamp as an occurrence chunk, `{run_width, run, seq}` (core §1.2: a run and a seq in Crockford's base32 in lowercase, 8 characters for a 16-bit run and 12 for a 32-bit one, the first of 12 `0` or `1`). An events key whose last chunk is no occurrence chunk, a ULID's among them, is refused."
